.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt OPENEIGRPD.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openeigrpd.conf
.Nd native OpenEIGRP named-mode configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is an initial-load, declarative named-mode EIGRP configuration.
Each directive occupies one line. Lines beginning with
.Sq #
or
.Sq !
are comments.
Nested scopes are closed with their corresponding
.Cm exit-*
command.
Only default-VRF IPv4 and IPv6 unicast address families are accepted.
This is a supported subset of named-mode EIGRP; it is not a generic
FRR or Cisco configuration interpreter.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm router eigrp Ar name
Open a named process; close with
.Cm exit .
The process accepts
.Cm shutdown
and
.Cm no shutdown .
.It Cm address-family ipv4|ipv6 Op unicast Op vrf default Cm autonomous-system Ar asn
Configure an AF and AS (1 through 65535); close with
.Cm exit-address-family .
Only
.Cm vrf default
is accepted when a VRF is given.
AF scope supports
.Cm eigrp router-id Ar A.B.C.D ,
.Cm shutdown ,
.Cm no shutdown
and
.Cm distance eigrp Ar internal external .
.It Cm network Ar IPv4-address Op wildcard
In an IPv4 AF, select matching interfaces.
An IPv4 prefix in CIDR notation is also accepted.
Noncontiguous wildcards are rejected.
This directive is not available for IPv6 AFs.
.It Cm neighbor Ar address interface
Configure a static peer in the enclosing AF.
.It Cm metric weights Ar tos k1 k2 k3 k4 k5 Op k6
Set the EIGRP metric weights in the enclosing AF.
.It Cm af-interface Ar interface
Open an interface scope; close with
.Cm exit-af-interface .
Supported controls include
.Cm bandwidth-percent ,
.Cm bandwidth ,
.Cm delay ,
.Cm hello-interval ,
.Cm hold-time ,
.Cm passive-interface ,
.Cm split-horizon ,
.Cm next-hop-self ,
.Cm shutdown
and their supported
.Cm no
forms.
.It Cm topology base
Open the base topology scope; close with
.Cm exit-af-topology .
Supported settings include
.Cm default-metric ,
.Cm variance ,
.Cm metric maximum-hops ,
.Cm maximum-paths ,
.Cm redistribute connected
and
.Cm redistribute static .
Redistribution can carry
.Cm metric Ar bandwidth delay reliability load mtu
and/or
.Cm route-map Ar name .
.It Cm ip|ipv6 prefix-list Ar name seq n permit|deny prefix Op ge n Op le n
Define a global prefix filter with first-match ordering and implicit deny.
.It Cm ip|ipv6 access-list Ar name seq n permit|deny prefix
Define a global destination-prefix ACL with first-match semantics and
implicit deny.
.It Cm route-map Ar name permit|deny n Op match ...
Define a global, first-match route-map clause.
Supported matches are
.Cm prefix-list ,
.Cm access-list
and
.Cm tag .
There are no
.Cm set
operations.
.It Cm distribute-list prefix|access Ar name in|out Op interface
Apply an AF-level distribution policy.
Undefined referenced policies deny rather than silently permit.
.It Cm key-chain Ar name key n secret plaintext
Define one authentication key per chain.
The file must be protected from group and other access.
An AF-interface uses both
.Cm authentication mode md5
and
.Cm authentication key-chain Ar name
to enable MD5 authentication.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
An IPv4 AS with interface participation and connected-route
redistribution:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
router eigrp campus
 address-family ipv4 unicast autonomous-system 4453
  eigrp router-id 192.0.2.1
  network 192.0.2.0 0.0.0.255
  af-interface eth0
   hello-interval 5
   hold-time 15
  exit-af-interface
  topology base
   default-metric 100000 10 255 1 1500
   redistribute connected
  exit-af-topology
 exit-address-family
exit
.Ed
.Pp
An IPv6 unicast AF (IPv6 participation is interface-based):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
router eigrp campus6
 address-family ipv6 unicast autonomous-system 6473
  eigrp router-id 192.0.2.1
  af-interface eth0
   hello-interval 5
  exit-af-interface
 exit-address-family
exit
.Ed
.Sh VALIDATION AND RELOAD
Validate a proposed file without changing routing:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openeigrpd-config -t -f /etc/openeigrpd.conf
openeigrpd -t -f /etc/openeigrpd.conf
.Ed
.Pp
The standalone validator tests syntax, not all runtime capabilities.
A live start applies the parsed plan through the actual semantic targets;
invalid runtime configuration fails startup rather than partially
activating an instance.
Signal
.Dv SIGHUP
is rejected with no live state change.
Restart
.Xr openeigrpd 8
after validating changes.
.Sh SECURITY
Keep key-bearing configuration files as root-owned regular files
with no group or other access bits, normally mode 0600.
The packaged service uses systemd credentials to make a protected copy
available to its unprivileged daemon user.
Do not pass secrets on the daemon command line.
.Sh UNSUPPORTED FEATURES
Nondefault VRFs, arbitrary nonbase topologies, route-map
.Cm set
actions, complex ACL syntax, HMAC-SHA-256, encoded type-7 secrets,
EIGRP Stub runtime and atomic live reload are not supported by this
native configuration path.
The source routing observer supports only default-VRF
.Cm connected
and
.Cm static
redistribution.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/openeigrpd.conf
Default configuration file.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openeigrpd 8 ,
.Xr oectl 8
